# Derived by hand from Semantics ch. 4 (R7: the new row at the end of the click's tick) and
# ch. 7 (round 3 ST: a gathered `for` publishes a tick after its rows moved): one row, then
# the click's new row at 1, whose key the gathered results take, published at 2.
test rows_gather_plain_results

tick 0
  added:
    0: Ui.Button(label="go")
    1/[0]/0: Ui.Label(text="i0=5")
    2: Ui.Label(text="1")

tick 1
  in:
    0: click
  added:
    1/[1]/0: Ui.Label(text="i1=7")

compute until idle: 1 tick, 2 to 2

tick 2
  changed:
    2: Ui.Label(text="2")
